details:
(a) the salient features and objectives of the Vigyan Jyoti Programme and whether districts in Andhra Pradesh have been covered under it through Jawahar Navodaya Vidyalayas;
(b) the nature of interventions provided to meritorious girl students under the programme there including exposure to premier scientific institutions, mentorship and role-model interactions; and
(c) whether any assessment has been made of the impact of such interventions on girl students' choice of STEM streams and career pathways and the plans to deepen this engagement, including extending the programme to more districts and government schools in the State?

(a) the current status of implementation of e-Courts Integrated Mission Mode Project across the country, including key initiatives undertaken under its ongoing phase; 
(b) whether the project has led to improvement in case management, digital filing and virtual hearings in courts; 
(c) the status of implementation of the project in Andhra Pradesh, including the number of courts computerised, digitised and integrated under the scheme in the State; and 
(d) the steps being taken to improve digital literacy and awareness among litigants and lawyers in the State to enable wider access to e-Courts services?

(a) whether preparatory activities for Census 2027, including House Listing and Housing Census, have commenced across all States and Union Territories;
(b) the State-wise status of digital infrastructure and self-enumeration facilities for Census, 2027;
(c) whether training programmes have been conducted for census functionaries and supervisors;
(d) whether any funds have been released to States and Union Territories for census-related activities; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the measures taken to strengthen Higher Education Institutions in Andhra Pradesh through accreditation support, research promotion, and the establishment of multidisciplinary Universities under NEP 2020;
(b) the progress made in integrating skill development and vocational courses into the higher education curriculum in the State;
(c) whether adequate career counselling and awareness mechanisms exist to help students, particularly first-generation and rural learners, meaningfully utilise flexible options such as multiple entry-exit and the Academic Bank of Credits; and
(d) the initiatives being taken to improve the Gross Enrolment Ratio and equity of access for disadvantaged groups in Andhra Pradesh?

(a) whether the ports of Andhra Pradesh, including Visakhapatnam and Krishnapatnam, have adopted action plans under the “Harit Sagar” Green Port Guidelines 2023, and if so, the details thereof;
(b) the specific green initiatives, such as renewable energy adoption, green hydrogen/LNG bunkering facilities, or waste management systems, undertaken at these ports so far;
(c) whether any of these ports have received Sagar Shreshtha Samman awards or been evaluated on Environmental Performance Indicators under the guidelines; and
(d) the targeted timelines set for achieving quantifiable reduction in carbon emissions at ports located in Andhra Pradesh?

(a) the details of the guidelines used in selecting heavy industry clusters for deployment of carbon mitigation systems under the newly announced ?20,000 crore CCUS Technology Fund;
(b) whether Government has established a specific emissions-reduction audit framework to assess the efficiency of carbon capture in selected pilot thermal power plants;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether Government proposes to issue standardized rules to enable Municipal Corporations to issue green bonds for the rejuvenation of urban wetlands; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the current status of implementation of underground cabling (UG) and Aerial Bunched (AB) cabling works undertaken in the State of Andhra Pradesh under the Integrated Power Development Scheme (IPDS), in place of conventional overhead lines;
(b) the extent of such cabling completed so far in the State, and the reasons for delay, if any, in the remaining sanctioned works; and
(c) the progress made in converting theft-prone, accident-prone, and coastal/cyclone-affected areas of the State to underground/AB cabling under the scheme?

(a) the targets set by Government for coal gasification by 2030 and the achievements made so far; 
(b) the category-wise funds sanctioned, number of projects approved and their location-wise details; 
(c) the details of Public Sector Undertakings (PSU)and private entities procuring coal for gasification purposes in the State of Andhra Pradesh; 
(d) whether any syngas production plants by PSU or private sector have been identified in the State, and if so, their location-wise details; and 
(e) the manner in which promotion of coal gasification supports States like Andhra Pradesh in the sectors of power, chemicals/fertilizers, steel and green hydrogen?

(a) the details regarding the number of drains constructed for safety purposes along railway tracks in Andhra Pradesh;
(b) the length of drains constructed and the locations identified as flood-prone or accident-prone stretches where such works have been undertaken;
(c) the details regarding the funds sanctioned, released and utilized for these drainage works, classified, year-wise and division-wise;
(d) whether Government has conducted any safety or vulnerability assessment to identify railway track sections requiring urgent drainage interventions in Andhra Pradesh; and
(e) if so, the criteria used for prioritization and the key findings of such assessments?

(a) the number of accelerators which have submitted Expression of Interest (EOI) under the SAMRIDH programme during the last five years in Andhra Pradesh, district-wise;
(b) the total number of accelerators which have been selected under the scheme during the last five years in Andhra Pradesh;district-wise;
(c) whether Government maintains the performance of these accelerators in the last five years; and
(d) if so, the list of startups supported under the programme by the selected accelerators, amount of funds allocated and disbursed to each accelerator in Andhra Pradesh, district wise?

(a) details regarding the skill development initiatives for women in emerging technologies such as Artificial Intelligence, Semiconductor design and renewable energy during the last five years, scheme-wise;
(b) details of the total number of women trained, certified and placed under such initiatives, year-wise, State-wise and district-wise for Andhra Pradesh;
(c) details of the total funds sanctioned, released and utilised for women-focused skill development programmes in emerging technologies during the last five years, year-wise and State-wise; and
(d) whether Government has taken steps to enhance participation of women from rural SC/ST/OBC in such programmes, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the status and timeline of finalisation and notification of the draft Floating Solar PV (FSPV) Potential Assessment Report and the draft Floating Solar Policy prepared by the National Institute of Solar Energy (NISE) and IIT Roorkee;
(b) the total floating solar potential identified across water bodies in the country under this assessment, State/UT-wise;
(c) whether the draft policy proposes a single-window clearance mechanism for floating solar projects involving multiple State departments and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the targets, if any, fixed for FSPV capacity addition by 2030?

(a) the progress made in implementing the Khelo Bharat Niti-2025 across States and Union-Territories and the mechanisms established to ensure effective coordination among Central Ministries, State Governments, National-Sports-Federations, educational institutions and other stakeholders;
(b) how Government is leveraging the Khelo Bharat Niti to strengthen India’s preparations for 2036 Olympic Games and the measures being taken to build a sustainable pipeline of medal-winning athletes across priority sporting disciplines; and
(c) the number of States and Union-Territories which have formulated, their sports policies in line with the vision and objectives of Khelo Bharat Niti?

(a) whether the Ministry has introduced any reforms to make recruitment to Government posts more efficient, transparent and time-bound;
(b) the measures taken to reduce the duration of recruitment process for the examinations conducted by the Union Public Service Commission (UPSC) and the Staff Selection Commission (SSC);
(c) whether any initiative has been launched to simplify the recruitment process and improve the experience of candidates; and
(d) the results achieved under these reforms?

(a) the current status and functioning of Employment Exchanges/Model Career Centres (MCCs) across the country;
(b) whether Government has assessed the effectiveness of these Exchanges/MCCs in facilitating placements, particularly in the private sector and if so, the findings thereof, and;
(c) the steps being taken by Government to strengthen these institutions and enhance private sector participation in job placements; and
(d) whether Government proposes to further integrate Employment Exchanges/MCCs with the National Career Service (NCS) portal to provide job-seekers with career counselling, skill mapping and real-time vacancy information and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the present status of Ocean Observation Network including Ocean Observation Buoys, Deep Sea Moorings and Coastal Observation Systems;
(b) the details of role of these observation systems in improving the forecasting of monsoon, cyclones and ocean conditions;
(c) whether any measures have been taken to expand and strengthen the Ocean Observation Network and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the manner in which real-time ocean observations are integrated with forecasting systems to improve weather and ocean forecasts?

(a) the current status of implementation of the PM SHRI Schools scheme, including the progress made in States like Andhra Pradesh where schools have already been selected under Phase-1; 
(b) whether Government proposes to expand the scheme to cover more schools in a phased manner, especially in rural and semi-urban areas, particularly in Andhra Pradesh; and 
(c) the steps being taken to ensure timely release of funds, teacher training and infrastructure upgradation so that selected schools can fully realise the objectives of the National Education Policy, 2020?

(a) the overall trend in CSR spending on education and skill-development activities across the country during the last three financial years and the share of total CSR funds directed towards this sector;
(b) the total CSR funds spent by companies specifically in Andhra Pradesh on education and skill-development activities during each of the last three financial years;
(c) the number of CSR-1 registered implementing agencies currently operating in Andhra Pradesh, including NGOs, trusts and Section 8 companies; and
(d) whether any Central scheme or guideline links corporate CSR funds to school infrastructure or skilling centres in Andhra Pradesh and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the major seminars, conferences and outreach programmes organised by the National Commission for Minorities during 2026; 
(b) the key research studies commissioned or completed by the Commission during the said period and their objectives; 
(c) whether the findings and recommendations of such studies have been considered for policy formulation or implementation of minority welfare programmes; 
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the measures taken to strengthen engagement with State Minorities Commissions and minority communities through institutional outreach initiatives?

(a) details of ongoing and pending railway projects in Andhra Pradesh as on date, including new lines, doubling, RUB/ROB and station redevelopment, project-wise;
(b) the current status of each project indicating year of sanction, estimated cost, expenditure incurred so far, physical progress and target date of completion;
(c) the total amount of funds sanctioned, released and utilised for these projects, project-wise;
(d) whether there are any long delays in completion of these projects, if so, the details and reasons thereof; and
(e) whether Government has taken any steps to expedite completion of these projects and ensure timely commissioning, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the details of the quantity and value of steel imported into the country during the last five years, including current year, category-wise, year-wise and country-wise;
(b) the quantity and value of steel exported from the country during the last five years including current year, year-wise, category-wise and destination-wise;
(c) the steel trade balance and the reasons for major changes in imports/exports, year-wise;
(d) whether Government has undertaken any measures to reduce import dependence and promote value-added steel exports, if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the details regarding the anti-dumping measures, quality control interventions implemented to regulate steel imports during the last five years?

(a) total length of rural roads constructed and number of habitations connected under various phases of the Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY) during financial year 2025-26;
(b) the plan for implementation of PMGSY during financial year 2026–27, particularly regarding upgradation and maintenance of roads, if any;
(c) the targets set for construction and upgradation of rural roads under the scheme, State-wise;
(d) whether any mechanism has been adopted to prioritize road connectivity in aspirational districts, tribal and remote regions, if so, details thereof; and
(e) the proposed investment for implementation of the scheme, including respective contributions of Centre and States, the details thereof?

(a) the progress made in the deployment of Kavach 4.0m, including the route kilometres and locomotives covered as of date;
(b) the railway zones and high-density corridors identified for implementation during 2026-27, State & district-wise including Uttar Pradesh;
(c) whether any timeline has been prescribed for network-wise deployment of Kavach, if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the measures taken to accelerate the installation and commissioning of Kavach across the Indian Railways network?

(a) the details regarding the incentives and support mechanisms in place by Government for development of One District One Product (ODOP) industries, including financial assistance, credit support, skill development, common facility centres, quality certification, branding and marketing support;
(b) the details of convergence of ODOP with other Central schemes such as MSME, PMFME, Skill India and export promotion programmes;
(c) the details of mechanisms adopted to facilitate market access for ODOP products, including e-commerce integration, domestic and international exhibitions, buyer–seller meets and export facilitation; and
(d) the details of outcomes of these initiatives including employment generation and exports under ODOP during the last five years, State/UT-wise?
